{"title":"datasette-agent 0.6a0","link":"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/15/datasette-agent/","date":1794714587000,"content":"\n    \n        <p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-agent/releases/tag/0.6a0\">datasette-agent 0.6a0</a></p>\n        <p>Accumulated small fixes for Datasette Agent, my agent plugin for Datasette that lets you ask questions about your data. Most notably, it now adds an agent prompt directly to the Datasette homepage, with support for hash-mentions of tables and queries:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Datasette homepage. Below the search box is a Datasette Agent heading with a text input and an ask button. User has typed: Tell me about #re - the box is showing autocomplete results for the repos and releases tables.\" src=\"/media/05dc7dade5f3ca3e1cc72852529e8bf7d8e918dc376feaaff25bd1d8d3f97773.webp\" /></p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-agent\">datasette-agent</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\">llm</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llms\">llms</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/ai\">ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/generative-ai\">generative-ai</a></p>\n    \n\n","author":"Simon Willison","siteTitle":"Simon Willison’s Weblog","siteHash":"1b599216bd27a00f15d67a3ed9719c64148630c70244b6dd8e743f17cb45527e","entryHash":"187875b4130951d9cad661075b3c9fe0e620ba85b3aa4e8d7b8a1b67ff81535c","category":"Tech"}